    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nI want to use`vi/` to do what looks like `vi?`but\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9688298860d8ac7d334139c5fd599edbedeff3c0/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1121C11-L1137C7\nassigns the `[\"?\"] = function() ... end `\n\nThe anonymous function is not easy to reuse, so it may be convenient to define this anonymous function as a function in `gen_spec` table, just like the `argument` function in this table.\n\nThis function can be named by other more reasonable name, maybe `query` or something else.",
