        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nHere is the version which works for 95% of use cases:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    ['/'] = function()\n      local left = vim.fn.input('Left edge: ')\n      local right = vim.fn.input('Right edge: ')\n      if left == '' or right == '' then return end\n      return { vim.pesc(left) .. '().-()' .. vim.pesc(right) }\n    end,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nI'd suggest using this directly, but as there is no easy way to make it \"properly\" dot-repeatable (right now it will ask left and right edge on every user prompt, which is not great) I'll think about adding a `gen_spec.user_prompt`.",
